0..78 Comment "// A record type\'s faces refused: one face holds a label the record lacks, and"
79..157 Comment "// one face is named twice. A reader `.#{` refused: it names a field or a face"
158..231 Comment "// that the record type lacks. Another reader fixes a field at a value of"
232..307 Comment "// another type. A record literal at a patched type states a fixed field at"
308..385 Comment "// another value, and so does a configuration coerced in to a patched type. A"
386..462 Comment "// system of faces names one face twice, and another system\'s faces disagree"
463..482 Comment "// where they meet."
483..485 Comment "//"
486..565 Comment "// A face lists only labels its record holds, and each face has its own name. A"
566..643 Comment "// reader `.#{` fixes only the fields its record type writes, and a face only"
644..722 Comment "// when the type member names it. A face\'s refusal covers its record and marks"
723..800 Comment "// the label, and the others stand at the second name or at the face. A fixed"
801..880 Comment "// value has its field\'s type, and a fixed field holds its reader\'s value. Each"
881..956 Comment "// of the two refusals stands at the value, the field or the configuration."
957..959 Comment "//"
960..1036 Comment "// The types stand in a module, whose members carry the verdict each refusal"
1037..1111 Comment "// states. Each refusal names the face and the record type. Two faces of a"
1112..1192 Comment "// system agree on their meet, and the refusal stands at the later face\'s value."
1193..1195 Comment "//"
1196..1277 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/record-faces.gandr` — the faces read, and the reader read"
1278..1359 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s faces refused"
1360..1370 Comment "//   alike"
1371..1437 Comment "// - see: #6504 — faces on lazy records and codata declarations."
